        "declaredIn": "default"
      },
      "holdsGraph": [
        "https://litlfred.github.io/cat-harness/0.1.0/ns#graphKind/methodology"
      ],
      "description": "The methodologies core adopts from its own corpus. Separate from `cat-harness/methodologies/` for the reason `smart-base-methodologies` is separate from both: a method belongs to the layer whose job it describes, so the directory lifts out with this instance and nothing else moves. Core's job, per this instance's AGENTS.md, is what a folio HOLDS, where it CAME FROM and how much is PRESENT — which is why a document-ingestion method is core's and not the harness's.",
      "readmePath": "methodologies/README.md",
